-- title:
--   Level-equivariance of the supersingular chart and its node annuli
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a natural number $M' \neq 0$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and a field $FSS$ that is an algebra over the residue field of $A$. Let $R$ be a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ to the field $F =$ `fieldBar q M'` with residue field $FSS$, i.e. a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers} \subseteq F$ lying over $A$ together with a surjective residue map onto $FSS$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal and which is compatible with the residue map of $A$. Assume: (hint) for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullback of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ along the level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is $R.\mathrm{integers}$ itself; $N$ is a finite set of places of $FSS$ over the residue field of $A$ with $\#N = q+1$, and $Dx$ assigns to each such place a set of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; (heqv) for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ of $FSS$ preserves $N$ setwise, and for $Q \notin N$ one has $\{P \mid \tau^{-1} \cdot P \in Dx\,Q\} = Dx(R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau \cdot Q)$; (htrans) the level automorphisms with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ act transitively on $N$ through $R.\mathrm{resAut}$; $An$ assigns to each place an `Annulus` of $F$ along $A$, and (hAn) for $\tau$ as above and $x \in N$ one has $\{P \mid \tau^{-1} \cdot P \in (An\,x).\mathrm{dom}\} = (An(R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau \cdot x)).\mathrm{dom}$; finally $C$ is a `ComponentChart` for $A$, $F$, $FSS$ with $C.\mathrm{integers} = R.\mathrm{integers}$ and with $C.\mathrm{dom}$ equal to the union of the $Dx\,Q$ over places $Q \notin N$. The conclusion has three parts: for all $\zeta$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, writing $\tau =$ `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`, the pullback chart $C.\mathrm{comap}\,\tau$ has the same valuation subring as $C$ and the same domain as $C$; and for every $x \in N$ there are $\zeta$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and an $x' \in N$ with $x' \neq x$ such that the domain of the pullback annulus $(An\,x).\mathrm{comap}(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta\ \gamma)$ equals the domain of $An\,x'$.
--
--   This is the transport step which turns the equivariance data attached to a semistable regular prolongation at a supersingular point into the three statements used later: level-invariance of the chart's valuation ring, level-invariance of its domain, and the fact that each of the $q+1$ node annuli is carried onto a different one by some level automorphism. It is used in the construction of a supersingular chart together with local affinoid and node annuli, including the special cases $q = 3$ and $q = 2$ with a divisibility assumption.
